<title>SINGAPORE: India buys aviation turbine fuel at $2.30-premium.</title>
<headline>India buys aviation turbine fuel at $2.30-premium.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has bought 25,000 tonnes of aviation turbine fuel by tender at a premium of $2.30 per barrel to MidEast spot quotes, on a cost-and-freight (c-and-f) basis, traders said on Monday.</p>
<p>The tender was awarded to Japanese trading house Marubeni International Petroleum Co (Mipco) and is for September 11-20 delivery to Goa or Kandla on the west coast, they said. The tender closed on August 29.</p>
